# ===== Tarkov food item descriptions (verbatim in-game text) =====
desc.can_gigabeef=A special edition, oversized can of GigaBeef, made to a traditional British recipe. Some say a meal of this quality even helps you think more clearly... though results may vary.
desc.can_condensed_milk=Condensed milk, also called "Sguschyonka" in Russia, once was a part of field ration for the Union soldiers in Civil War, but later reached unprecedented popularity in post-Soviet countries, becoming almost a staple product. Canned, it can be stored for decades and remain just as sweet, tasty and nutritious.
desc.can_tushonka=A large amount of canned beef stew, commonly referred to as "tushonka", can be stored for years, thus rivaling condensed milk in importance as a food supply for both military and tourists.
desc.can_green_peas=Can of green peas, rich in vitamins and selenium, which makes it especially valuable in the dubious environmental conditions of the Norvinsk region.
desc.can_sprats=Delicacy sprats from the Alconafter company.
desc.can_duck_pate=A spreadable meat product made from cooked ingredients, produced by Norvinsk Poultry Plant. No ducks were harmed in the making. Probably.
desc.can_squash=A can of squash spread, a little vegetable treasure that goes well with almost anything and boasts an impressive set of vitamins and minerals.
desc.bar_alyonka=The famous milk chocolate of post-Soviet times, sweet and creamy.
desc.bar_slickers=A sweet nutritional bar for a quick bite. Well balanced in proteins, fiber, and vitamins, but a bit over the top in sweetness.
desc.pack_sugar=A packet of lump sugar. A rare thing in conditions of total food shortage. It is also used in brewing.
desc.jar_devildog=This "DevilDog's" brand mayonnaise is quite famous in Tarkov. Recommended to use with boiled potatoes.
desc.bottle_moonshine=A first-class moonshine straight from the Hideout. Sixfold distillation, purification, crystallization, and ionization of the boiling process led to the creation of this 79-degree drink. Remember that drinking alcohol can lead to tragic consequences.
desc.bottle_vodka="Tarkov fire water". It is not recommended to consume it in general, alcohol is harmful and all that, but sometimes it is necessary to relax after the battle. No need to raid area 51 to see them aliens after all.
desc.bottle_whiskey=The most popular whiskey among the PMCs. The unique filtration of the drink occurs through charcoal obtained from the burning of Samara sugar birch. This is an alcohol drink, and alcohol is harmful. Especially for such a warrior like you.
desc.bottle_beer=Mmmmm... Pevko. The legendary drink of the streets of Tarkov.
desc.croutons_emelya=Emelya rye croutons with assorted flavors were a favorite snack for kids and "cracking open a cold one while watching movies" enjoyers. Although, these days you won't find either the kids or any movies in Tarkov.
desc.bread_baguette=A traditional French baguette baked in full compliance with the 1993 French Bread Decree. Many TerraGroup employees were willing to take quite a detour on their way to work just to pick one up. It's easily recognized by the distinctive "Cocaoo_" stamp the baker marked on every loaf.

